OL,3,GNEWSAOne in five baby deaths
OL,4,A'potentially avoidable' - report
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than one in five baby deaths in
OL,7,Fthe UK were "potentially avoidable had
OL,8,Fdifferent care been given", a report
OL,9,Fhas found.
OL,11,FAn annual review conducted by the
OL,12,FNational Perinatal Epidemiology Unit at
OL,13,Fthe University of Oxford collated
OL,14,Finvestigations into the deaths of 4,110
OL,15,Fbabies in 2025.
OL,17,FPublished this week, the report
OL,18,Fidentified at least one issue with
OL,19,Fmaternity care in 93% of fatalities,
OL,20,Fwith those problems potentially
OL,21,Faffecting the outcome of 21% of cases.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,339,330,200,160,0,100
